                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "236458733",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198136910753",
                            "num_reviews": 12,
                            "playtime_forever": 68,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 35,
                            "last_played": 1790710613
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "RICO is a fun roguelike shooter with a SWAT-style gameplay loop. You clear rooms, collect evidence, destroy assets, and deal with bombs and other threats.\n\nMy first run definitely didn’t go as planned since I failed the case, but I still had a good time with it. The randomly generated levels also give the game some replayability.\n\nThe movement can feel a bit awkward, though. There’s no jump option, and some obstacles can block your movement in ways that feel frustrating. The ADS on some weapons, like the MP9, can also be annoying because the muzzle flash makes it difficult to see what you’re shooting at.\n\nVisually, the game reminds me a lot of the Borderlands series, which I personally like.\n\nOverall, RICO is a solid and enjoyable shooter, but it doesn’t do anything particularly groundbreaking.",
